Actually, grid bugs *do* multiply, but the built-in limitations on monster
multiplication keeps them from doing very much of it.  All (or almost all)
multiplying monsters call a routine called clonemon(), which turns one
monster into two monsters each with *half* of the original's hit points.
Fractions round down, to further limit multiplication.  I'm not sure, but I
think they *could* heal up back to their original maxhit, thus potentially
becoming infinite (only really likely with gremlins).  Grid bugs don't
multiply much because they have so few hit points to begin with, and a 1HP
critter doesn't split.
